{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123221","id":4449854172,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCTti3A","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123221","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123221.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123221.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123221","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123221/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123221/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123221/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/39e1f57583d28bbc88a28a7508fc9d80d5e8883d","number":123221,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Core]: Add a simple backoff strategy to SpinLock","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Helps with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/65404\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nBasically `ObjectDB::get_instance` is a major hot spot that is under super high contention any time threads are used, especially in editor as it constantly uses `Variant::get_validated_object` to check for valid objects.\r\n\r\nThe backoff could be more complex, but as far as I know if we could use `std::atomic_wait` from C++20 it will use the most efficient strategy by default, so this is just a simple stop-gap until C++20 is awailable.\r\n\r\nShould also help in other places `SpinLock` is being used, which seems to be mainly `GLOBAL_GET_CACHED`, not sure if any of them are placed in the place they could be called from several threads to cause contention.\r\n\r\n### Benchmark\r\n\r\nUses the same benchmark as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/85167\r\n\r\nCompile command used: \r\n```\r\nscons target=template_release optimize=speed accesskit=no use_llvm=yes linker=lld production=yes\r\n```\r\n\r\nSystem:\r\n> Godot v4.8.dev (4b03d5558) - EndeavourOS `#1` SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:18:59 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors (1920x1080 @ 165.00 Hz, 1920x1080 @ 60.01 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 (nvidia; 610.57.04) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-9300H CPU @ 2.40GHz (8 threads) - 15.49 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\r\n\r\nSmaller number is better.\r\n\r\n```json\r\n[\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"category\": \"Core > Object Db\",\r\n\t\t\"name\": \"12 Threads Full Contention\",\r\n\t\t\"results\": {\r\n\t\t\t\"time\": {\r\n\t\t\t\t\"old\": 606.5,\r\n\t\t\t\t\"new\": 376.2,\r\n\t\t\t\t\"old_div_new\": 1.6121743753322701\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t},\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"category\": \"Core > Object Db\",\r\n\t\t\"name\": \"12 Threads Half Contention\",\r\n\t\t\"results\": {\r\n\t\t\t\"time\": {\r\n\t\t\t\t\"old\": 324.0,\r\n\t\t\t\t\"new\": 268.4,\r\n\t\t\t\t\"old_div_new\": 1.2071535022354696\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t},\r\n\